.bd
SUBROUTINE
.in +5
.br
.bd
strchr
- find first occurrence of a character
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
C
.in +5
.br
.bd 3
char *strchr(s, c)
char *s;
char c;
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
FUNCTION
.in +5
.br
strchr returns a pointer to the first occurrence of the
character c in the string s.  The terminating null is
considered part of the string, so strchr(s, '\0') returns a
pointer to the terminator.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
RETURNS
.in +5
.br
a pointer to c in s, or 0 if c does not appear.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
NOTES
.in +5
.br
index is the pre-ANSI name for strchr; the two are the same
routine.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
